<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Sign in with Apple. Required by App Store Guideline 4.8 because
	     the app offers Google Sign-In.

	     This file existing is not enough on its own. Two more things must
	     be true or the button fails at runtime with an unhelpful
	     authorization error:

	       1. The Xcode target must reference it. Open Runner.xcworkspace,
	          select the Runner target, Signing & Capabilities, and add
	          "Sign in with Apple". Xcode wires CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS to
	          this file. Doing it in Xcode rather than by hand-editing
	          project.pbxproj is deliberate — that file is easy to corrupt
	          and hard to review.

	       2. The App ID in the Apple Developer portal must have the Sign
	          in with Apple capability enabled, and the provisioning
	          profile must be regenerated afterwards. Codemagic fetches a
	          fresh profile on every build, so it picks this up on its own
	          once the App ID is updated.

	     Supabase also needs its Apple provider configured (Services ID,
	     Team ID, Key ID and the .p8 key) or the token exchange fails
	     after Apple has already shown its sheet — which looks to the user
	     like the app broke at the last step. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>

	<!-- External Link Account Entitlement, granted by Apple Developer
	     Relations on 3 September 2026 for com.anuragrishi.knowthyself
	     (it reverses the 27 August denial). It permits a SINGLE neutral
	     link out to our website for account creation and management — no
	     price, no buy button, no promotion in the app.

	     Same two out-of-code steps as Sign in with Apple above, or the
	     link fails at runtime / review:
	       1. Enable "External Link Account" on the App ID in the Apple
	          Developer portal, then let the provisioning profile
	          regenerate (Codemagic fetches a fresh one per build).
	       2. The Xcode target must reference this entitlements file
	          (already true for Sign in with Apple).

	     The destination URL lives in Info.plist under SKExternalLinkAccount
	     and MUST match externalAccountUrl in
	     lib/core/config/purchase_config.dart, or App Review's
	     binary-vs-plist check rejects it. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.storekit.external-link.account</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
